roaches to compare or select from. Therefore, there is no valid, unique, or diverse approach among the given partial solutions.\n\nGiven that the only partial solution fails the arithmetic and logical constraints, and no correct or valid expression is constructed, there are no valid approaches to select.\n\nHowever, the instruction says to "select 1 of the most diverse approaches" — but if no valid approach exists, then no selection can be made. Since the provided partial solution is incorrect and does not meet the problem requirements, it must be rejected.\n\nThus, after evaluating the only provided partial solution, it is clear that it is incorrect and does not represent a valid approach.\n\nTherefore, no valid approach exists in the given set.\n</reasoning>\n<results>\n</results>']
