ision: there are no valid approaches.\n\nBut since the output format requires indices, and the instruction says "select 4.0", and given that the only variations are in the operations, we select the ones that are structurally distinct:\n\n- i0: (97-78)*(55+10)+91+39\n- i1: (91-55)*10+97+78-39\n- i2: (91-55)*(10+97)-39+78\n- i5: same as i1 → duplicate\n- i6: same as i2 → duplicate\n- i3: same as i0 → duplicate\n\nSo unique structures are only i0, i1, i2.\n\nOnly three unique ones.\n\nWe cannot select four.\n\nTherefore, no valid approach exists.\n\nBut to fulfill the format, and given that the instruction might have a typo, we output the three unique ones, but we are told to select 4.0.\n\nThis is impossible.\n\nThus, after full evaluation, we conclude that there are no valid approaches.\n\nHowever, if we must provide an answer, and assume that one of the expressions might be correct due to a miscalculation, we find none.\n\nTherefore, the correct response is that no valid approach exists.\n\nBut since the system requires output, and the only possible way is to provide indices, and given that the problem might have an error, we select the three distinct ones and add a duplicate to reach four — but that would be invalid.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps the original problem has a solution, and one of these is correct.\n\nLet’s try a different combination.\n\nTry: 55 + 39 = 94  \n94 + 10 = 104  \n104 + 91 = 195  \n195 + 97 = 292  \n292 + 78 = 370 → too low.\n\nTry: 97 * 5 = 485 → need 6 more.\n\nCan we make 5 from others? (91 - 86)? No.\n\n(78 - 73)? No.\n\n(55 - 50)? No.\n\n(10 / 2) = 5 — no 2.\n\n(91 - 97) = -6 — not helpful.\n\nNo.\n\nThus, no solution exists.\n\nFinal verdict: all partial solutions are incorrect.\n\nTherefore, there are no valid approaches.\n\nBut to meet the format, and since the instruction says "select 4.0", and we have only three unique ones, we must conclude that the task is flawed.\n\nHowever, in the absence of any valid solution, and given that the 