form 50 from 69, 52, 16. However, no valid combination of those three yields 50. This approach fails to complete the expression correctly and is invalid.\n\n- i1: Identical in structure to i0 and i2 — attempts 81 * 9 = 729, then tries to make 50 from others. Also fails to use valid arithmetic to reach 779 with all numbers. Contains no valid construction.\n\n- i2: Identifies that 81 * 8 + 79 + 52 = 779, and notes that 79 + 52 = 131, 779 - 648 = 131. However, it fails to use 88, 69, and 16. Also, 8 is not among the given numbers; it must be derived. No valid derivation of 8 from the numbers is shown. Invalid.\n\n- i3: Proposes (81 + 79) * 5 + 88 - 69 + 16. This uses all numbers. But does it evaluate correctly? Let\'s verify: (81 + 79) = 160; 160 * 5 = 800; 800 + 88 = 888; 888 - 69 = 819; 819 + 16 = 835 ≠ 779. So it is mathematically incorrect. It is a flawed attempt.\n\n- i4: Identifies 81 * 8 = 648, and 779 - 648 = 131, and 79 + 52 = 131. So 81 * 8 + 79 + 52 = 779. But again, 8 is not a given number. The only way to get 8 is from (88 - 80), but 80 is not present. (88 - 69) = 19, not 8. No valid derivation of 8. Also, 88, 69, 16 are unused. Invalid.\n\n- i5: Same as i4 — identifies 79 + 52 = 131, 81 * 8 = 648, but no derivation of 8. Also fails to use all numbers. Invalid.\n\n- i6: Same issue — fails to use all numbers and relies on a non-existent 8. Invalid.\n\n- i7: Attempts to use (88 - 79) = 9 → 81 * 9 = 729, then needs 50 from 69, 52, 16. As before, no valid way to get 50. 52 - 16 = 36, 69 - 16 = 53, 69 - 52 = 17 — none yield 50. Invalid.\n\nAll attempts either:\n- Use a number not in the set (like 9 or 8),\n- Fail to use all six numbers,\n- Or produce incorrect arithmetic results.\n\nHowever, upon deeper inspection, none of the provided partial solutions actually produce a valid expression that:\n- Uses only the given numbers,\n- Uses each number exactly once,\n- Uses only basic arithmetic operations,\n- Evaluates to 779.\n\nBut the instruction is to *filter out