aches.\n\nFirst, analyze each solution:\n\n- i0: Proposes a solution: "89 + 73 + 56 - 94 - 75 + 84 = 133" and verifies it step-by-step. The arithmetic is correct:  \n  89 + 73 = 162  \n  162 + 56 = 218  \n  218 - 94 = 124  \n  124 - 75 = 49  \n  49 + 84 = 133 → valid.  \n  The expression uses all six numbers exactly once. This is a correct, valid arithmetic expression.\n\n- i1: Proposes (89 + 75) - (94 - 84) + (73 - 56).  \n  Compute:  \n  89 + 75 = 164  \n  94 - 84 = 10  \n  73 - 56 = 17  \n  164 - 10 = 154  \n  154 + 17 = 171 ≠ 133 → incorrect.  \n  Also, the solution attempts to use all numbers but the result is wrong. Incorrect approach.\n\n- i2: States "89 + 75 - 84 + 56 - 94 + 73 = 133" and gives it as the answer.  \n  Compute:  \n  89 + 75 = 164  \n  164 - 84 = 80  \n  80 + 56 = 136  \n  136 - 94 = 42  \n  42 + 73 = 115 ≠ 133 → incorrect.  \n  This expression does not evaluate to 133. Incorrect.\n\n- i3: Proposes (89 - 75) * (94 - 84) + 56 + 73 - 84 + 84.  \n  This uses 84 twice: once in (94 - 84), once at the end. Invalid — violates "each number at most once". Also, the expression is malformed. Incorrect.\n\n- i4: Proposes (89 + 75) - (94 - 84) + (73 - 56).  \n  This is identical in structure to i1 — same expression, same incorrect result (171). Redundant and incorrect.\n\n- i5: Identical to i2 — "89 + 75 - 84 + 56 - 94 + 73 = 133" — already evaluated as incorrect (115). Duplicate of i2.\n\n- i6: Attempts to use (84 - 75) = 9, (56 / 9) ≈ 6.22, etc., but fails to reach 133. Also, no valid expression is fully formed or verified. Contains no correct path. Incorrect and incomplete.\n\n- i7: Proposes (89 + 75) - (94 - 84) + (56 - 73).  \n  Compute:  \n  89 + 75 = 164  \n  94 - 84 = 10  \n  56 - 73 = -17  \n  164 - 10 = 154  \n  154 + (-17) = 137 ≠ 133 → incorrect.\n\nNow, group by core logic:\n- i0 is the only one that correctly evaluates to 133 and uses all numbers exactly once. It uses a simple linear combination with addition and subtraction.\n- i1, i4, i7 use